Original content
----------------

Prism’s original expression — citizen copy, methodology notes, documentation,
templates as written, and named derived work on official series already in a
vintage (“Analysis by Prism”) — is licensed under Creative Commons
Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0):

    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/

You may share and adapt that original expression if you give appropriate
credit and license adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0. Attribution does not imply
that Prism or a producing office endorses your use.

When you reuse a Prism derivation, keep the producer cite next to it. Name
the derivation as Prism’s; do not replace the agency as producer. Highest,
lowest, ranks, and comparable frames stay bound facts from the vintage — not
a partisan report card.


No extra restriction
--------------------

These licences are the grant. The vision and editorial rules describe how
Prism itself is built and published. They are not additional legal terms on
reuse of the Software or of Prism’s original expression.
